/// Write a bitstring to nonvolatile ram.  (V36)
///
/// Write a bitstring to the nonvolatile ram.
///
/// # Synopsis
///
/// Error = WriteBattMem( Buffer, Offset, Len )
/// D0                    A0      D0      D1
///
/// ULONG WriteBattMem( APTR, ULONG, ULONG );
///
/// # Arguments
///
/// * Buffer          Where to get the bitstring. Offset          Bit offset of first bit to write. Len             Length of bitstring to write.
///
/// # Returns
///
/// Error           Zero if no error.
///
/// # Notes
///
/// The battery-backed memory is checksummed. If a checksum error
/// is detected, all bits in the battery-backed memory are
/// silently set to zero.
/// Partial byte writes (less than 8 bits) result in the bits
/// written being read from the low-order bits of the source byte.
///
/// # Bugs
///
/// Whether a write is observable depends on the machine backing battmem, not on the call.
/// Measured on two emulated machines writing the three-bit SCSI host-ID field at offset 65:
/// the A4000 reads the written value back, while the A1200 returns success and discards it,
/// reading back the original. Every step reports error 0 on both. Treat a zero return as
/// "the resource accepted the request", not as proof the bits were stored, and read back if
/// the stored value matters.
@library("battmem.resource")
extern pub fn WriteBattMem(buffer: *u8, offset: u32, length: u32) -> u32
